---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const EFFECTIVE_DATE = 'May 4, 2026';
const COMPANY = 'Orbital Software, LLC';
const APP_NAME = 'Orbital';
const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'privacy@example.com';
const WEBSITE = 'https://example.com';
---

<style>
  .page-wrapper {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 2rem 2rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .effective-date {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--gray);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  hr {
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--primary-light);
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }
</style>

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Orbital"
  description="How Orbital collects, uses, and protects your data."
>
  <div class="page-wrapper">
    <a class="back-link" href="/"><span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span> Back to Orbital</a>

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="effective-date">Effective date: {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

    <p>
      {COMPANY} ("we", "us", or "our") operates the {APP_NAME} mobile application
      and the {WEBSITE} website (collectively, the "Service"). This Privacy Policy explains
      what information we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

    <p><strong>Account information.</strong> When you create an account we collect your email address and any profile details you provide.</p>

    <p><strong>Contact data you add.</strong> {APP_NAME} lets you store and manage information about the people in your network — names, emails, phone numbers, notes, and similar details. This data is yours; we store it on your behalf to power the Service.</p>

    <p><strong>Usage information.</strong> We may collect information about how you interact with the Service (features used, screens visited, actions taken) to understand how the app is being used and improve it.</p>

    <p><strong>Crash and diagnostic reports.</strong> If the app crashes or encounters an error, we may automatically collect diagnostic data including device type, OS version, and a stack trace to help us fix the problem. We use Sentry for error monitoring; see <a href="https://sentry.io/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sentry's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <p><strong>Payment information.</strong> If you subscribe to a paid plan, payment is processed by our payment provider. We do not store your full card number or payment credentials — only a record of your subscription status.</p>

    <p><strong>Device and log data.</strong> We automatically receive information your device sends, such as IP address, browser type, and referring URL, when you access the Service.</p>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Provide, maintain, and improve the Service</li>
      <li>Authenticate you and keep your account secure</li>
      <li>Diagnose crashes and fix bugs</li>
      <li>Process payments and manage your subscription</li>
      <li>Send you transactional emails (account notices, receipts)</li>
      <li>Respond to your support requests</li>
      <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <p>We do not sell your personal information or the contact data you store in {APP_NAME}.</p>

    <h2>3. Data Sharing</h2>

    <p>We share information only in these limited circumstances:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Service providers.</strong> We use third-party vendors (hosting, error monitoring, payments) who process data on our behalf under confidentiality obligations.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal requirements.</strong> We may disclose information if required by law, subpoena, or to protect the rights and safety of our users or others.</li>
      <li><strong>Business transfers.</strong> If {COMPANY} is acquired or merges with another company, your information may be transferred as part of that transaction. We will notify you before your data is subject to a different privacy policy.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Data Retention</h2>

    <p>
      We retain your account and contact data for as long as your account is active. If you request deletion
      (see Section 6), we will delete your data within 30 days, except where we are required to retain it
      for legal or legitimate business reasons.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Security</h2>

    <p>
      We use industry-standard measures to protect your data, including encrypted connections (HTTPS/TLS)
      and access controls. No method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure, and we cannot
      guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your Choices and Rights</h2>

    <p>You may:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access or correct</strong> your account information from within the app.</li>
      <li><strong>Request deletion</strong> of your account and associated data by emailing <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We will process your request within 30 days.</li>
      <li><strong>Opt out</strong> of non-essential communications by following the unsubscribe link in any email.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or California, you may have additional
      rights under GDPR, UK GDPR, or CCPA respectively. Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> to exercise those rights.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>

    <p>
      The Service is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information
      from children under 13. If you believe we have inadvertently collected such information, please
      contact us and we will delete it promptly.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>

    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the effective date
      at the top of this page. For material changes, we will notify you by email or a notice within the app
      before the change takes effect.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Contact Us</h2>

    <p>
      Questions about this Privacy Policy? Reach us at:<br />
      <strong>{COMPANY}</strong><br />
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
